        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(agents): sessions_search tool for full-text recall over past session transcripts",
        "body": "Closes #100978\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where an agent had no way to answer \"what did we decide about X last month?\" from its own past conversations. `sessions_list` filters metadata only, `sessions_history` needs an already-known session key, and `memory_search`'s session corpus is an experimental opt-in that requires an embeddings provider — so on a default install past session content was unsearchable for the agent.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a core `sessions_search` agent tool backed by a SQLite FTS5 index in the existing per-agent database (next to the memory index tables). Indexing is event-driven: user/assistant text enters the index after each successful transcript append (index failures never affect the append), and the first search per process runs one bounded background reconcile for pre-existing transcripts, crash gaps, and orphan cleanup — searches never poll transcript files. Search executes gateway-side behind a new additive `sessions.search` method that accepts a bounded session-key allowlist (≤200 keys, one owning agent per call), so a tool call resolves to a single FTS query per agent instead of per-session fan-out; the same seam can later serve Control UI session search (#81583, #100712). Visibility, sandbox restrictions, and snippet redaction mirror `sessions_history` exactly, and hidden hits are dropped before limits/byte caps are applied. No new config surface; tool availability follows the existing tool policy. Tool results, reasoning blocks, and images are not indexed; only the transcript's active branch is searchable. CJK trigram tokenization is a documented follow-up.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgents can now recall their own prior conversations: `sessions_search` returns bounded, redacted snippets with `sessionKey`, timestamp, and role, and the agent follows up with `sessions_history` for full context. Works out of the box — no embeddings provider, plugin, or config needed. Agents only ever see sessions they could already read via `sessions_history`. New docs page: `docs/concepts/session-search.md`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox (delegated, exit 0): focused suite across 11 test files — indexer (append/backfill/branch rewind/replacement/orphan cleanup), tool (visibility filtering, sandbox `restrictToSpawned`, alias handling, redaction, limit/byte caps, single-RPC regression for multi-session visibility), gateway param validation + one-agent scoping, protocol schemas, embedded stub, plugin-SDK transcript runtime, tool catalog/mutation/replay-safety registrations, and system-prompt snapshot stability. Run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28831632122\n- Remote typecheck lanes (`tsgo:core`, `tsgo:core:test`): pass.\n- Structured autoreview (Codex, gpt-5.5) on the full bundle: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Prompt snapshots regenerated (`prompt:snapshots:gen`); docs map regenerated (`docs:map:gen`); Kysely types regenerated from the schema SQL.\n",
